    "gold_solution": "```python\nfrom gurobipy import *\n\ndef solve_problem():\n    m = Model(\"Battlefield_Logistics\")\n    m.setParam(\"TimeLimit\", 100)  # Set time limit to 100 seconds\n\n    # Data\n    depots = list(range(3))  # D0..D2\n    units = list(range(4))  # U0..U3\n    supplies = list(range(3))  # S0..S2\n    days = list(range(1))  # Day0..Day0\n\n    demands = [[[35.58], [23.63], [30.0]], [[10.03], [10.73], [34.61]], [[43.97], [32.75], [21.66]], [[30.6], [13.37], [32.6]]]\n    depot_supplies = [[[36.78], [28.09], [47.1]], [[37.77], [30.78], [59.41]], [[49.82], [22.59], [57.68]]]\n    transport_costs = [[3.88, 1.44, 4.0, 3.7], [2.68, 3.61, 2.07, 3.06], [4.35, 3.84, 4.93, 4.61]]\n    risk_costs = [[128.03, 79.74, 145.68, 182.7], [62.21, 177.48, 159.82, 182.26], [177.09, 175.94, 104.89, 106.17]]\n    supply_volumes = [1.6, 1.56, 0.67]\n    penalty_costs = [75.35, 82.65, 95.79]\n    vehicle_cost = 10.0\n    vehicle_capacity = 55.0\n    total_vehicles = 19\n\n    # Decision variables\n    # Flow_D{d}_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}: Amount of supply s from depot d to unit u on day t\n    flows = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                for s in supplies:\n                    flows[(d, u, s, t)] = m.addVar(lb=0.0, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Flow_D{d}_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Slack_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}: Shortage of supply s at unit u on day t\n    slacks = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for u in units:\n            for s in supplies:\n                slacks[(u, s, t)] = m.addVar(lb=0.0, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Slack_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Veh_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}: Number of vehicles on route d->u on day t\n    vehicles = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                vehicles[(d, u, t)] = m.addVar(lb=0.0, vtype=GRB.INTEGER, name=f\"Veh_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Route_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}: Route d->u is active on day t (binary)\n    routes = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                routes[(d, u, t)] = m.addVar(vtype=GRB.BINARY, name=f\"Route_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Objective: Minimize total cost (transport + penalty + vehicle + risk)\n    obj = quicksum(\n        transport_costs[d][u] * flows[(d, u, s, t)]\n        for t in days for d in depots for u in units for s in supplies\n    )\n    obj += quicksum(\n        penalty_costs[s] * slacks[(u, s, t)]\n        for t in days for u in units for s in supplies\n    )\n    obj += quicksum(\n        vehicle_cost * vehicles[(d, u, t)]\n        for t in days for d in depots for u in units\n    )\n    obj += quicksum(\n        risk_costs[d][u] * routes[(d, u, t)]\n        for t in days for d in depots for u in units\n    )\n    m.setObjective(obj, GRB.MINIMIZE)\n\n    # Depot capacity constraints: Total outflow <= supply\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for s in supplies:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    quicksum(flows[(d, u, s, t)] for u in units) <= depot_supplies[d][s][t],\n                    name=f\"DepotCap_D{d}_S{s}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Demand constraints: Inflow + slack >= demand\n    for t in days:\n        for u in units:\n            for s in supplies:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    quicksum(flows[(d, u, s, t)] for d in depots) + slacks[(u, s, t)] >= demands[u][s][t],\n                    name=f\"Demand_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Vehicle capacity constraints: Total volume <= vehicles * capacity\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    quicksum(supply_volumes[s] * flows[(d, u, s, t)] for s in supplies) <= vehicle_capacity * vehicles[(d, u, t)],\n                    name=f\"VehCap_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Route activation constraints: vehicles <= total_vehicles * route\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    vehicles[(d, u, t)] <= total_vehicles * routes[(d, u, t)],\n                    name=f\"RouteAct_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Fleet size constraints: Total vehicles <= total_vehicles\n    for t in days:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(vehicles[(d, u, t)] for d in depots for u in units) <= total_vehicles,\n            name=f\"FleetSize_Day{t}\"\n        )\n\n    m.optimize()\n    return m\n```",
    "LLM_description": "Situation:\nThree supply depots\u2014Supply Depot Bravo (western corridor), Depot Sierra (central rail/road hub), and Depot Delta (eastern airstrip)\u2014must sustain four forward units: 3rd Infantry Battalion at FOB Alpha, Armored Squadron Phoenix at COP Ridge, Artillery Battery Lima at Fire Base Hammer, and Recon Troop Echo at Patrol Base Falcon. Required commodities include ammunition, fuel, and rations. The terrain is restrictive; valley routes are exposed to indirect fire and IEDs, mountain passes are narrow and subject to rockfall, and the central highway experiences periodic interdiction. Weather and road conditions limit convoy speeds and dictate daylight movement windows. Escort teams and route-clearance assets are limited and must be prioritized.\n\nMission:\nDeliver required supplies to all forward units within the current operational cycle while minimizing total operational cost, balancing transport costs, vehicle deployment costs, shortage penalties, and fixed route security risk costs.\n\nExecution/Concept:\n- Prioritize unit resupply based on operational tempo and survivability, consolidating loads where practical to reduce movements.\n- Assign flows from each depot to each unit by supply type, constrained by depot stock availability and unit demand. Any controlled shortfall is recorded and penalized.\n- Vehicles are allocated by route; each vehicle\u2019s carrying capacity governs how much can be delivered per movement. The fleet size is finite and must be apportioned across all active routes.\n- Routes remain inactive unless deliberately activated. Activating a route\u2014sending any vehicles on it\u2014incurs a fixed Risk Cost representing security overhead (escort teams, route clearance, overwatch, QRF staging), charged once per route for the operational period regardless of the number of vehicles deployed on that route.\n- Vehicles may only move on routes that are activated. Activation decisions should favor bundling shipments to exploit the fixed security overhead while avoiding activation of low-value routes unless required by demand or risk mitigation.\n- Transport costs vary by depot-to-unit pairing and are combined with vehicle deployment costs, shortage penalties, and fixed route security risks in the objective function. The plan may accept limited shortfalls at low-risk/low-cost units when risk and transport costs exceed penalty thresholds.\n- Movement Control Team will sequence convoys, synchronize escorts and engineers for route clearance, and maintain deconfliction with fire support. Alternate routing and backhaul opportunities will be used to optimize fleet utilization without violating security constraints.\n\nAnnex A - Logistics Data:\nUnit Demands (Units x Supplies):\nUnit\\Supply | S 0 | S 1 | S 2\n-----------------------------\nU 0        |  35.58 |  23.63 |  30.00\nU 1        |  10.03 |  10.73 |  34.61\nU 2        |  43.97 |  32.75 |  21.66\nU 3        |  30.60 |  13.37 |  32.60\nDepot Supplies (Depots x Supplies):\nDepot\\Supply | S 0 | S 1 | S 2\n------------------------------\nD 0        |  36.78 |  28.09 |  47.10\nD 1        |  37.77 |  30.78 |  59.41\nD 2        |  49.82 |  22.59 |  57.68\nTransport Costs (Depot x Unit):\nDepot\\Unit | U 0 | U 1 | U 2 | U 3\n----------------------------------\nD 0        |   3.88 |   1.44 |   4.00 |   3.70\nD 1        |   2.68 |   3.61 |   2.07 |   3.06\nD 2        |   4.35 |   3.84 |   4.93 |   4.61\nRisk Costs (Depot x Unit):\nDepot\\Unit | U 0 | U 1 | U 2 | U 3\n----------------------------------\nD 0        | 128.03 |  79.74 | 145.68 | 182.70\nD 1        |  62.21 | 177.48 | 159.82 | 182.26\nD 2        | 177.09 | 175.94 | 104.89 | 106.17\nPenalty Costs per Unit Shortage: [Supply S0: 75.35, Supply S1: 82.65, Supply S2: 95.79]\nVolume per Supply Unit: [Supply S0: 1.6, Supply S1: 1.56, Supply S2: 0.67]\nFleet Parameters: Cost 10.0, Capacity 55.0, Total 19",
    "LLM_description_template": "Situation:\nThe brigade combat team is conducting sustained operations in mountainous terrain with contested ground lines of communication. Supply Depot Bravo, Logistics Hub Charlie, and Ammunition Point Delta hold mixed stocks of ammunition, fuel, and medical materiel. Forward elements\u2014including the 3rd Infantry Battalion at FOB Saber, the 1st Armored Company near Assembly Area Hammer, the Artillery Battery at Firing Point Echo, and the Forward Surgical Team at FOB Mercy\u2014require immediate resupply during the current operational day. Main supply routes traverse narrow valleys and exposed ridgelines vulnerable to ambush and improvised explosive hazards. Airlift is constrained by weather and air defense threats, placing the burden on ground convoys.\n\nMission:\nDeliver required classes of supply from the depots to forward units within the current operational day while minimizing total operational cost (transport, shortage penalties, vehicle deployment, and fixed route security risk costs) and maintaining force readiness.\n\nExecution/Concept:\n- Source and Demand: Flows from each depot cannot exceed stocks on hand by supply type and day. Unit demands are to be met to the maximum extent; controlled shortfalls are permitted but incur readiness penalties.\n- Vehicle Capacity and Loading: Cargo assignments must respect vehicle capacity limits; supply items have different volume factors, which drive load planning and the number of vehicles required per route.\n- Route Activation and Security Overhead: Ground movement will occur only on routes that are formally activated. Activating any route triggers a fixed Risk Cost representing escorts, route clearance, ISR overwatch, and QRF posture\u2014this cost is incurred once per active route per day, regardless of how many vehicles use it. Vehicles may only operate on activated routes.\n- Fleet Management: The total number of vehicles deployed across all routes cannot exceed the available fleet. Vehicle employment on any origin\u2013destination pairing is constrained by route activation and overall fleet limits.\n- Cost Considerations: Transportation costs vary by origin\u2013destination pairing and reflect distance, terrain, and condition. Each deployed vehicle adds to operational cost. Shortfalls incur penalty costs reflecting mission impact. Fixed Risk Costs apply to each active route independent of convoy size.\n- Course of Action: Prioritize life-sustaining and mission-critical supplies, consolidate shipments to reduce the number of activated routes, and draw from the most proximate or best-stocked depots to limit transport and vehicle costs. Avoid fragmenting flows across multiple high-risk corridors unless required to meet capacity or survivability constraints. The selected plan will balance demand satisfaction against transport costs, fixed security overhead, and fleet utilization to minimize total cost.\n\nAnnex A - Logistics Data:\n{DEMANDS}\n{DEPOT_SUPPLIES}\n{TRANSPORT_COSTS}\n{RISK_COSTS}\n{PENALTY_COSTS}\n{SUPPLY_VOLUMES}\nFleet Parameters: Cost {VEHICLE_COST}, Capacity {VEHICLE_CAPACITY}, Total {TOTAL_VEHICLES}"
}